WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.610
This is the singularity... one day at a time.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.150
Here's the last 24 hours in AI. Sorry... SI.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.760
Today, AI left the chat: Claude designed proteins against scorpion venom,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.370
and two real labs confirmed 17 of them.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.500
And OpenAI bought Orchestra Bio,

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.700
whose AI agents keep drug development on schedule.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.090
Models: this week,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.160
four Google DeepMind agents beat Minecraft on their own. It took 27 hours.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.430
DeepSeek gave away its engine for running AI faster and cheaper,

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.110
on Nvidia or Huawei chips.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.950
ChatGPT now lets you lock private chats behind a 4-digit PIN, or your face.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.410
And Gemini got in the car: ask it,

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:58.020
"What's my flight gate?" And it finds the answer in your Gmail.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.280
Money: SpaceX's AI business grew ninefold,

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.350
to $7.6 billion in a quarter. Bigger than Starlink.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.070
The Wall Street Journal says Anthropic brought in $16 billion in six months.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.120
A year earlier, about $1 billion.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.710
Reuters says ByteDance,

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.310
Alibaba and Tencent ordered over $35 billion of Nvidia cards.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.810
And Amazon will invest over €16 billion in Germany next year,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.420
in cloud, AI and satellite internet.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.460
Humans: Spotify cut over 50 million AI slop and spam songs from recommendations,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.440
putting human artists first.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.280
And this week,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.660
Lightroom on your phone learned to open closed eyes in a photo, with one tap.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.460
The catch: researchers found over 6,800 links to people's shared Meta AI chats.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.020
And Korean AI firm Elice sank 30% on its first day.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.210
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.170
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.060
Machines: Waymo's driverless taxis are coming to Madrid, with riders next year.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.520
Tractor maker AGCO will try Digit humanoid r

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.600
obots on its Kansas factory floor next year.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.170
Eka's robot arm feels what it grabs: 1,500 picks an hour. A person, about 600.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.980
AI left the chat today: into labs, cars and factories.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.330
The future isn't on a screen anymore. It's out here.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.040
Every day, the curve gets steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.510
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.530
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.910
This has been the singularity, one day at a time.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.870
Feel the SI.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.680
Want the whole month? Join Peter Xing live in Sydney on October 30.
